From: Justin Pfister <119864532+JJRPF@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:09:12 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/37] tools/aurora-sep: idle-ab: settings for a list of CPUs

pd-always@4-9 and wfi-only@0-3 apply the setting to the listed CPUs and
leave the others with both states, to tell the E cores' share of the
saving from the P cores' or one cluster's. Each window's log line gets
every CPU's CPU PD residency. A CPU that does not exist is refused
before anything is written.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AuzUDcEeRJQ6RCdWW2XWLb
